# Dance Dance Revolution 4th Mix Plus Solo (G*A34 VER. JBA), Konami 2000: the first boot, with the install cassette in the slot (MAME: -cassette install; HIRAKU:
# --cassette install). The 573 BIOS boots the CD, which first asks to update the CD-ROM drive's
# firmware (NOTE 604, "Press test switch"); Test starts the update and the install, the CD to the
# onboard flash, then to the PC Card in slot 2: INFO 506, installation completed, by frame ~22,800.
# Hashes the main RAM every frame and snapshots every 60 frames, to compare with MAME.
game ddr4mps

hash ram  0x80000000 0x80400000   # 4 MiB main RAM (KSEG0)

at 600 press "Service Mode" 8
from 0 every 60 snap
at 24000 quit
